&io;
// Self method calls: a bare `NAME(...)` dispatches to a method of the current
// instance. The old explicit `self.NAME(...)` form is retired — the `self.`
// prefix is no longer written for a method call.
// 自调用：裸 `NAME(...)` 即派发到当前实例的方法。旧的显式 `self.NAME(...)` 形式已
// 退役——方法调用不再写 `self.` 前缀。
//   - dispatch:  twice(21)          (a method of the current instance)
//   - dispatch:  greet()            (likewise)
// `self.` still reads members — it is just no longer needed to call a method:
// a member field is reached as `self.field`.
// `self.` 仍可读取成员——只是调用方法不再需要它：成员字段写作 `self.field`。
// Input/output parameters are usable variables you operate on directly:
// `answer << x` publishes x as the output.
// 输入 / 输出参数都是可直接操作的变量：`answer << x` 把 x 公布为输出。
$Program {
    @::[() -> () {
        -(io::OStream out);

        out << "twice(21) = ";
        out << twice(21);

        out << " | greet() = ";
        -(std::String g) << greet();
        out << g;
    }];

    // Identity method: echoes its input. Demonstrates that the input param
    // `x` and the output param `answer` are ordinary, directly-operable
    // variables (no `=:`/`<<` ceremony needed just to read them).
    // 恒等方法：回显输入。证明输入参数 x 与输出参数 answer 都是可直接操作的
    // 普通变量。
    @twice[(x[std::Number]) -> (answer[std::Number]) {
        answer << x;
    }];

    @greet[() -> (msg[std::String]) {
        msg << "hello from self";
    }];
};
